(39, 'ronyroy@oemails.com', NULL, NULL, 'Subject: Urgent: FEMA Compliance Verification Required for Inward Remittance', '<p>Dear Customer,</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">This is to inform you that the funds received in your account are currently under review as part of the mandatory regulatory verification process.</span></p><p>Considering the substantial volume of inward remittances received, the transaction is being examined in accordance with the applicable provisions of the Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA). FEMA compliance verification is an integral part of the regulatory review process for such transactions.</p><p>As per the internal regulatory procedures of the NBFC, a prescribed FEMA declaration form is required to be duly completed, signed, and submitted along with the necessary supporting documentation for completion of the verification process.</p><p><br></p><p>This communication is being shared on an urgent basis to ensure timely completion of the required FEMA compliance formalities. As per applicable regulatory guidelines and compliance requirements, the required form and supporting documents must be submitted to us at the earliest for verification and record purposes.</p><p>Please note that failure to submit the required FEMA compliance documentation may result in restrictions on your account. You may be unable to carry out transactions, and any future inward remittances may not be credited until the verification process is completed.</p><p>You are requested to complete and submit the required FEMA compliance documentation immediately to avoid any delay in completion of the verification process.</p><p><br></p><p>Regards,</p><p>Compliance Department</p><p>[ DECCAN FINANCE LTD ]</p>', 'support@deccanfinltd.world', 'SUCCESS', NULL, '2026-07-08 16:23:08'),
